---
description: Complete features from implementation and relevant automated or simulator checks; defer physical-device validation to the maintainer
alwaysApply: true
---

# Feature completion

- Mark an implemented feature complete after appropriate automated checks and
  feasible build/simulator verification pass. Physical-device validation is not
  a prerequisite for feature completion or a merge-ready feature PR.
- The maintainer owns physical-device testing and any resulting tweaks. Track
  those checks separately as deferred follow-up; do not leave working features
  incomplete solely for that reason.
- Keep implementation gaps and observed failures actionable. Do not invent
  measured performance, accessibility or hardware results for deferred tests.
- Separate feature status, additional validation coverage, and distribution or
  publishing approval. This policy does not authorize publication or merging.
- Apply the same distinction in FEATURE_CHECKLIST.md, documentation and PR bodies.
